mothershipOS: the example sensors HAL's proximity sensor reports "far" (its maximum range) instead of a constant
2.5, which Android reads as covered: SystemUI's falsing classifier rejected lock screen swipe-ups
(ProximityClassifier percentInProximity=1.0, "the swipe jumps back unless pulled far") and in a call the screen would
turn off. Until the phone's real sensors reach the VM, nothing is near the screen.

diff -ruN a/sensors/aidl/default/Sensor.cpp b/sensors/aidl/default/Sensor.cpp
--- a/sensors/aidl/default/Sensor.cpp	2026-11-17 23:25:52.420693117 +0100
+++ b/sensors/aidl/default/Sensor.cpp	2026-11-17 23:25:52.437234111 +0100
@@ -333,7 +333,9 @@
 };
 
 void ProximitySensor::readEventPayload(EventPayload& payload) {
-    payload.set<EventPayload::Tag::scalar>(2.5f);
+    // mothershipOS: "far" (the maximum range). 2.5 (< maxRange) read as permanently covered: SystemUI's falsing
+    // classifier rejected lock screen swipes (percentInProximity=1.0) and calls would blank the screen.
+    payload.set<EventPayload::Tag::scalar>(mSensorInfo.maxRange);
 }
 
 GyroSensor::GyroSensor(int32_t sensorHandle, ISensorsEventCallback* callback) : Sensor(callback) {
